/**

@page page_peano_runtime_analysis Runtime analysis

\tableofcontents

Peano applications can emit runtime and load-balancing statistics through their
standard logging output. These records are the basis for postprocessing scripts
that inspect tree sizes, remote-cell counts, rank balance, and time spent in
different phases of a run.

For load-balancing analysis, dump the program output into a file and inspect the
`toolbox::loadbalancing::LoadBalancer::getLocalLoadBalancing()` records. They
report local and remote cell counts per tree, which is usually enough to identify
overdecomposition or badly balanced subpartitions.

For ExaHyPE-specific timing and scaling scripts, see
@ref page_exahype_runtime_analysis.

*/
